Directory Opus 4.x - ChangeLog
==============================

Newest version first.  Earlier versions, up to 4.16, were released by
Jonathan Potter (GP Software) and Jacek Rzeuski; see biz/dopus on Aminet.


4.17 (unreleased)
-----------------

Built from the GPL sources of 4.16 with vbcc, vasm and vlink, for the
68020 without FPU instructions.  Needs Kickstart 3.0 or newer.

Versions: DirectoryOpus 4.17, dopus.library 22.19, ConfigOpus 4.14i,
DOpus_Disk 2.5, DOpus_Icon 1.7i, DOpus_Print 1.29, DOpusRT 4.7.

New:
- Clock bar: free memory can be shown in megabytes, e.g. "FAST:118.4M"
  (ConfigOpus, System/Clocks, "Show free as: Megabytes free").
- Iconified window: the same option, e.g. "F:118.4M".
- French catalogs, recovered from the 4.16 binary release.
- English help files from the 4.16 release (the help in the 4.16 sources
  was German), plus the translated help for deutsch, espanol, francais,
  italiano, polski and suomi.

Changed:
- Files are copied in large chunks (up to 1 MB) also when the copy
  progress indicator is on.  Before, they were read in 8 KB packets,
  which was much slower on fast disks.  AsyncIO is no longer used.
- The clock's CPU usage is measured by sampling 50/60 times a second
  whether the CPU is busy.  Without sysinfo.library the old figure
  counted task switches and showed 30-40% on an idle machine.
- Menu items are drawn with the screen's menu colours (BARBLOCKPEN,
  BARDETAILPEN) instead of fixed pens; a custom text colour is kept.
- About requester: "Modified by Andrzej Rogozynski".

Fixed:
- A read error during a copy was treated as success, so the copy could
  miss data.  A short write (e.g. disk full) now fails the copy too.
- The lister could stop reacting to clicks when the mouse wheel scrolled
  fast past the top or bottom of a list (also in 4.16).
- NewMouse wheel events could throw away queued mouse clicks.
- The memory fields of the clock bar had no fixed width, so the text
  moved whenever a number changed length.  On machines without Fast RAM
  the "Bytes" display looked as if Fast RAM were present.
- DOpus_Icon: the Icon Information window closed again as soon as it
  opened (an array too small for its 15 shortcut keys, also in 4.16).
- Catalogs: German config strings that were hidden by a syntax error,
  stray German entries, and English texts that had drifted from the
  program.
